# NEVER commit samples. These lines are load-bearing.
#
# Extension rules alone cannot do this job. The bundled fixture `invoice.pdf`
# is a PE wearing a document extension, which is the exact case this tool
# exists to detect, so a rule keyed on the extension waves it straight
# through. The magic-byte check in .githooks/pre-commit is the real defence.
# The lists below are the cheap first pass.

# Sample and output directories. `cli.py samples` writes fixtures wherever it
# is pointed, and the README points it at ./demo, so the conventional names
# are ignored wholesale rather than file by file.
samples/
demo/
corpus/
scratch/
out/
output/
reports/

# Backstop for samples written outside those directories.
*.bin
*.exe
*.dll
*.sys
*.vir
*.elf
*.so
*.dylib
*.o
*.obj
*.com
*.scr
*.msi
*.cab
*.iso
*.img
*.dmp
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz
*.tar

# Scan output. Reports embed the absolute path of every file scanned, so they
# carry the directory layout and the username of the machine that produced
# them. Working files, not artefacts to publish.
report.json
*.jsonl
maltriage-*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
venv/
.venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
